{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review: Gerrit change 1704 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1704), commit ad9d08b806 on branch bluebottle-enrich-lock, based on merged origin/main c6828ef348.\n\nLocal gate status at push: all runnable scripts/check_*.py gates 0 (including comment-hygiene and the wall-clock-assert gate), complexity baseline --check active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0, all four generators re-run with no diff (gen_cli_reference regenerated docs/cli-reference.md from the pinned help text src/rebar/_cli/help/doctor.txt), make lint green, make typecheck green (519 files), commit-message wrap gate passed, verify-commit-ticket OK, DCO gate 0.\n\nTargeted test evidence: tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py 29 passed (9 of them new for the lock), tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py 14 passed (3 rewritten for the drain leg), and the three existing lock-owner suites 41 passed UNTOUCHED — the regression guard proving the _stamp_is_stale extraction preserved _mkdir_lock_is_stale byte-for-byte.\n\nThe full CI-parity pytest invocation is still running locally on a heavily loaded host (it had reached 29% after ~40 minutes, crawling through the facade parity suite). Rather than block on it I pushed so CI's Verified gate — the authoritative run — executes in parallel; the local run continues as a cross-check and any red from either gets fixed before submit. No ticket close will happen before Verified +1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786599514066765001,"uuid":"c96c3343-a6a4-47ea-aef0-53ce5cb0fc12"}